globalThis.RoyaleIdeReadme = "# royale-ide\n\nA Royale IDE, itself written in Royale (Jewel) and compiled by the\n`royale-ts` port. It builds Royale apps **entirely in the browser, with no\nserver**:\n\n- **File explorer + tabbed Ace editor** for the project's sources (MXML/TS/CSS).\n- **Virtual file system (VFS)**: the project's files live in an in-memory map\n  seeded from `project-data.js` and persisted to `localStorage` (survives a\n  page reload; **Reset** re-seeds from the generated data).\n- **In-browser build**: *Run* posts the VFS to a Web Worker that runs the\n  royale-ts compiler + terser in memory and answers with **one self-contained\n  HTML document** (all CSS inlined, one classic-script bundle). The preview\n  iframe shows it via `srcdoc` — no URLs, no cache, no network.\n- **Debug** (unminified bundle) and **Release** (terser-minified bundle +\n  minified CSS) builds; keyboard: Ctrl/Cmd+S save, Ctrl/Cmd+Enter run,\n  Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Enter run release.\n\nThe default project is `sample-project/` (a counter demo). Its files are\nbaked into the generated data, so the IDE works as a purely static site.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nroyale-ide/\n  royale.json                 IDE build config (entry, namespaces, cssBundle, …)\n  sample-project/             the default project shown in the IDE\n  src/main/royale/            IDE sources: App.mxml + components/ (AceEditor,\n                              DynamicSplitView, Iframe)\n  src/main/resources/         staged into dist/ as-is:\n    index.html                loads project-data.js + the app module\n    App.css, assets/          IDE styling + Ace assets\n    scripts/compiler-worker.js  the build worker (importScripts the generated stack)\n    generated/                *** generated by tools/gen-data.mjs — do not edit ***\n  tools/gen-data.mjs          generates the browser-side compiler data\n  tools/rehearse-worker.mjs   sandbox dress rehearsal (no browser needed)\n  smoke.py                    end-to-end smoke test (serves dist/, drives Chrome)\n  dist/                       build output (the deployable static site)\n```\n\n## Generating all needed components\n\nEverything is generated from the repo root. Three stages:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Build the royale-ts compiler (only if royale-ts sources changed).\ncd royale-ts && npm run build && cd ..\n\n# 2. Generate the IDE's browser-side compiler data:\n#    royale-ide/src/main/resources/generated/*.js\nnode royale-ide/tools/gen-data.mjs\n\n# 3. Build the IDE -> royale-ide/dist\nnode royale-ts/out/cli/main.js build royale-ide\n```\n\nStage 2 produces the six generated assets that make the compiler\nbrowser-capable (the compiler core is synchronous and Node-free; these fold\nin the host-bound pieces):\n\n| asset               | content                                                                 |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `typescript.js`     | TypeScript 4.9.5 UMD compiler API (sets `globalThis.ts`)                |\n| `ts-shim.js`        | minimal `ts.sys` browser stand-in (`newLine` is load-bearing)           |\n| `tslib-data.js`     | all TypeScript lib `*.d.ts` by bare name (`RoyaleTsLib`)                |\n| `compiler.js`       | royale-ts compiler core + terser + @jridgewell, one classic script (`RoyaleCompiler`) |\n| `frameworks-data.js`| framework sources + module dirs + component manifests (`RoyaleFrameworks`) |\n| `project-data.js`   | the default project's files + parsed royale.json (`RoyaleSeedProject`)  |\n\n**Re-run stage 2 (then stage 3)** whenever the compiler, the frameworks tree,\nor `sample-project/` changes — the generated data is a snapshot.\n\n## Included projects & licenses\n\nThe IDE's own code (`App.mxml`, `components/`, `tools/`, `sample-project/`,\n`ts-shim.js`) is written for this project. It is built with **Apache Royale**\n(the AS3 framework, Apache License 2.0), whose TypeScript port is\n`royale-ts/` (compiler + `frameworks/`). The build folds in these third-party\nprojects:\n\n| project | version | license | lands in |\n| ------- | ------- | ------- | -------- |\n| [TypeScript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) (Microsoft) | 4.9.5 | Apache-2.0 | `generated/typescript.js`, `generated/tslib-data.js` |\n| [terser](https://github.com/terser/terser) (orig. Mihai Bazon) | 5.51.2 | BSD-2-Clause | `generated/compiler.js` |\n| @jridgewell source-map tools (6 packages, see below) | — | MIT | `generated/compiler.js` |\n| [Ace Editor (ace-builds)](https://github.com/ajaxorg/ace) | 1.44.0 | BSD-2-Clause | `dist/scripts/ace.js`, `mode-javascript.js`, `theme-chrome.js`, `worker-*.js` |\n| [dialog-polyfill](https://github.com/GoogleChrome/dialog-polyfill) (The Chromium Authors) | 0.4.9 | BSD-3-Clause | `dist/scripts/dialog-polyfill.min.js`, `dist/css/dialog-polyfill.min.css` |\n\n<details><summary>@jridgewell source-map tools (all MIT)</summary>\n\n- `@jridgewell/source-map` 0.3.2\n- `@jridgewell/trace-mapping` 0.3.17\n- `@jridgewell/gen-mapping` 0.3.2\n- `@jridgewell/set-array` 1.1.2\n- `@jridgewell/sourcemap-codec` 1.4.14 (original author: Rich Harris)\n- `@jridgewell/resolve-uri` 3.1.0\n\nAll by Justin Ridgewell.\n</details>\n\nNotes:\n\n- The vendored **terser** is a patched fork: it exposes a synchronous\n  `minify_sync` (upstream is generator-based) so the worker can minify without\n  an event loop. The BSD-2-Clause terms are unchanged.\n- **dialog-polyfill** ships as a third-party asset of the Royale *Basic*\n  framework; the Jewel theme references it, so the IDE build stages it to\n  `dist/`. (The framework also carries optional `material-icons` 4.0.0\n  (Apache-2.0) and `font-awesome` 5.15.4 (SIL Open Font License 1.1) assets\n  for other themes; the Jewel theme does not reference them, so they are not\n  staged here.)\n- Full license texts: the framework's third-party licenses are staged at\n  `royale-ts/frameworks/assembly/third-party/<name>/<version>/LICENSE-*`, and\n  each npm dependency's `LICENSE` lives under `royale-ts/node_modules/`.\n\n## Running\n\nThe IDE is a static site; any static file server works:\n\n```bash\ncd royale-ide/dist && python3 -m http.server 7071\n# -> http://127.0.0.1:7071\n```\n\nThe first *Run* pulls the ~19 MB compiler stack into the worker\n(one-time, then cached); each sample-project build takes ~15 s.\n\n## Testing\n\n```bash\n# Full end-to-end: serves dist/ itself, drives headless Chrome\n# (shell -> debug build -> interactive preview -> release build -> clean console).\n/home/neon/play_env/bin/python3 royale-ide/smoke.py\n\n# Fast dress rehearsal (no browser): loads the generated stack + worker in a\n# bare sandbox and runs a debug + release build of the sample project.\n# Previews land in royale-ide/.rehearsal/ (gitignored).\nnode royale-ide/tools/rehearse-worker.mjs\n\n# Compiler test suite (royale-ts).\ncd royale-ts && npm test && cd ..\n```\n";
